NEWOS DOOM port - 0001-compile-as-gnu99-on-newos-libc

Reason: the released sources do not compile under NEWOS.

am_map.c declares three variables with the storage class but no type
("static nexttic", "register outcode1"), which was legal in the pre-ANSI
K&R-and-gcc-extension sense NEWOS' cross compiler does not accept, and
-Werror turns the diagnostics into a build failure.

doomdef.h enables SNDSERV, which routes all sound through a separate
"sndserver" process that NEWOS neither builds nor launches. With the
define off, the engine calls I_UpdateSound()/I_SubmitSound() inline and
the NEWOS i_sound.c answers them.

Apply from inside the extracted linuxdoom-1.10/ directory: patch -p1 < this-file

